WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:03.430
Abraham: Cyber security is
extremely important especially

00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:04.860
when it comes to sensitive data

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:07.740
And there are three main
types of sensitive data that

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:09.180
hackers tend to exploit?

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:16.569
These are Personal Information, Business
Information, and Classified information.

00:00:17.289 --> 00:00:20.950
If these are accessed by cyber
criminals, it could be disastrous for

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:25.460
individuals, companies, organisations
and governments accordingly.

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:30.050
Nicole: Cyber-attacks can lead to the
illegal distribution of sensitive data

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:36.320
via the dark web, including personally
identifiable information [PII], protected

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:41.440
health information [PHI], personal
information, intellectual property,

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:43.430
or industry information systems.

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:47.650
It is extremely important that
sensitive data must always be

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:51.550
protected and inaccessible to all
who are not permitted to see it.

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:56.559
Restrictions on access of personal
or an organisation’s sensitive data,

00:00:56.840 --> 00:01:01.669
needs to be robust especially when
it pertains to individual privacy and

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:06.479
property rights and even more so when
it involves areas of national security.

00:01:07.539 --> 00:01:09.479
Abraham: Let’s have a
look at this more closely.

00:01:10.459 --> 00:01:14.420
Sensitive data that includes
PII [Personally identifiable

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:20.090
information], PHI [Protected health
information] and personal information,

00:01:20.429 --> 00:01:22.360
is held by many organisations.

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:27.430
It may be low level or high level and
should be kept secure accordingly.

00:01:27.969 --> 00:01:32.000
Nicole: Personal Identifiable
Information [PII] is information

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.840
that can be used by a cybercriminal
to identify or locate an individual.

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:42.000
This could be a name, address, phone
numbers, data of birth, IP address,

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:46.890
location details, or any other
physical or digital identity data.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:50.280
Think about how much of
this data is shared online

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:52.050
especially through social media.

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:55.729
Birthday details, age, phone number etc.

00:01:56.260 --> 00:01:59.979
and then think about what could happen
if this data got into the wrong hands.

00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:03.950
The less personal details and
information shown on social

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:08.340
media, the less PII information
is available to cyber criminals.

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:13.620
Abraham: Protected Health Information
[PHI] is [PII] that has been

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:15.550
collected through healthcare services.

00:02:16.179 --> 00:02:20.550
This may relate to physical or mental
health of an individual, their access to

00:02:20.559 --> 00:02:25.370
health care services, and any information
about their health status, including

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:31.000
medical histories, test results, mental
health information and even case studies.

00:02:32.389 --> 00:02:35.600
PHI could be stolen by hackers
and sold or ransomed until the

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:39.900
healthcare organisation pays a fee
if they not adequately protected.

00:02:40.109 --> 00:02:43.620
Nicole: Personal information in
the UK is covered by GDPR G.D.P.R.

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:47.930
and all personal data must be
processed securely using the

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:49.870
appropriate organisational measures.

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:54.950
To make sure this happens companies
must consider risk analysis regarding

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:59.470
the safety of data both physical
and digital, making sure that all

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:01.950
data is kept secure and encrypted.

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:05.999
Abraham: There are many kinds of
cyber security incidents but those

00:03:05.999 --> 00:03:09.790
that involve personal data breaches
need to be reported to the ICO

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:14.830
[Information commissioners office]
within 72 hours of becoming aware of it.

00:03:15.549 --> 00:03:18.419
If this affects an individual’s
rights and freedoms, then they

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:19.910
must also be told without delay.

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:24.030
Nicole: Where appropriate this will be
shared with the National Cyber security

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:30.350
centre [NCSC] and other law enforcement
and cyber crime agencies or regulators

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:35.260
such as NCA National Crime Agency [NCA],
the Financial Conduct Authority [FCA],

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:39.739
and the Payment Cards Industry [PCI].

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:43.260
Abraham: A key principle of the UK
General Data protection regulation

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:47.619
is that personal data is processed
securely and means that all systems

00:03:47.679 --> 00:03:51.870
and services should have the correct
security to maintain confidentiality.

00:03:51.969 --> 00:03:56.530
Nicole: Intellectual property is defined
as the creation of something, that

00:03:56.530 --> 00:04:01.950
could be an invention, literary work,
artistic work, designs, symbols and images

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:06.920
that are used in everything around us,
including our websites and domain names.

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:12.040
The access, distribution of and
or use of without permission is

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:16.079
classed as intellectual property
crime and falls under cyber crime.

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:21.700
Intellectual property needs to be
protected by cyber security as when

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:25.529
private data is gained and sold
on, it can lead to counterfeiting,

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:32.310
database rights issues, trademark and
copyright misuse, impersonation etc.

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:38.090
Intellectual property usually belongs to
the author or creators of the asset, but

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:42.810
it belongs to an employer if the asset
is created whilst under their employment.

00:04:43.469 --> 00:04:47.210
If a third party creates something
for another organisation the

00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:50.840
intellectual property rights will
be with the third party but, the

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:55.370
responsibility for its safety will also
remain with the other organisation.

00:04:56.059 --> 00:05:00.310
Abraham: There are two important pieces
of legislation concerning IP rights.

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:06.900
The Copyright Design and Patents Act
1988 [CDPA] deals with copyright,

00:05:06.940 --> 00:05:11.220
including copyright in databases,
and defines what a database is.

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:16.830
The Copyright and Rights in
Databases Regulations 1997 [CRDR]

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:19.320
establishes what database rights are.

00:05:20.530 --> 00:05:23.509
Nicole: Information systems
are present in most industries.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:25.450
Finance and insurance,

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:31.460
Education, Health services, Manufacturing,
Telecommunications, Data processing and

00:05:31.460 --> 00:05:34.239
hosting and Government agencies of course.

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:38.050
Abraham: Common types of
information systems are ‘transaction

00:05:38.050 --> 00:05:42.039
processing’, ‘management
information’, ‘decision-support’,

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:44.110
and ‘executive support’ systems.

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:48.270
Poor security in information
systems can leave an organisations

00:05:48.270 --> 00:05:50.200
systems and services at risk.

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:54.850
It is therefore very important that
cyber security is in place at all levels.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:06:00.440
Cyber security here involves personal
information in most cases and GDPR

00:06:00.449 --> 00:06:02.350
compliance is a legal requirement.

